(43, '5d2f85c3-1ff5-4893-b15d-d1fe4e863d1d', '9781593353452', 'The Godfather', NULL, 'Mario Puzo', 'Koch, Neff & Oetinger & Co', 'OL48593945M', '1969', 'chi', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 450, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'The Godfather is a crime novel by American author Mario Puzo. Originally published in 1969 by G. P. Putnam\'s Sons, the novel details the story of a fictional Mafia family in New York City (and Long Beach, New York), headed by Vito Corleone. Puzo\'s dedication for The Godfather is \"For Anthony Cleri\". The novel\'s epigraph is by the French author Honoré de Balzac: \"Behind every great fortune there is a crime.\" The novel covers the years 1945 to 1955 and includes the back story of Vito Corleone from early childhood to adulthood.\r\n\r\n\r\n----------\r\nAlso contained in:\r\n\r\n - [The Godfather / The Fortunate Pilgrim](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7920005W)\r\n - [The Godfather / The Last Don](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1673242W)', 'The Godfather is a crime novel by American author Mario Puzo. Originally published in 1969 by G. P. Putnam\'s Sons, the novel details the story of a fictional Mafia family in New York City (and Long Beach, New York), headed by Vito Corleone. Puzo\'s dedication for The Godfather is \"For Anthony Cleri\". The novel\'s epigraph is by the French author Honoré de Balzac: \"Behind every great fortune there is a crime.\" The novel covers the years 1945 to 1955 and includes the back story of Vito Corleone from', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Detective and mystery stories, Organized crime, Criminals, Italian Americans, Mafia, Fiction, Criminals in fiction, Drama, Italian Americans in fiction, Mafia in fiction, Organized crime in fiction, Romance, Corleone family (Fictitious characters), English fiction, Crime, fiction, Criminals, fiction, Italian americans, fiction, New york (n.y.), fiction, Fiction, mystery & detective, general, Corleone family (Personajes literarios)', 1, '2026-07-20 23:50:03', '2026-07-20 23:50:03'),
(44, '990cf4b9-fa37-4877-9ec6-a36bd4162897', '9788433961259', 'Seta', NULL, 'Alessandro Baricco', 'Canongate Books Ltd', 'OL60092006M', '1920', 'lit', 'Romans', 'history', 'paperback', 'all', 125, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'France, 1861. When an epidemic threatens to wipe out the silk trade in France, silkworm breeder Herve Joncour has to travel overland to distant Japan, out of bounds to foreigners, to smuggle out healthy silkworms. In the course of his secret negotiations with the local baron, Joncour\'s attention is arrested by the man\'s concubine, a girl who does not have oriental eyes. Although they are unable to exchange so much as a word, love blossoms between them.', 'France, 1861. When an epidemic threatens to wipe out the silk trade in France, silkworm breeder Herve Joncour has to travel overland to distant Japan, out of bounds to foreigners, to smuggle out healthy silkworms. In the course of his secret negotiations with the local baron, Joncour\'s attention is arrested by the man\'s concubine, a girl who does not have oriental eyes. Although they are unable to exchange so much as a word, love blossoms between them.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Novela italiana, Fiction, Travel, French, Italian, History, Romance, Self-discovery, Silk industry, Fiction, romance, historical, Japan, fiction, Fiction, romance, general, Literature, Cuentos de amor, Industria y comercio, Historia, Seda, Ficción, Cuentos eróticos, Comerciantes', 1, '2026-07-20 23:50:06', '2026-07-20 23:50:06'),
