(140, 'f294882c-c73d-4e1c-b82d-fca1e31ae80f', '9781409021551', 'The Confession', NULL, 'John Grisham', 'R. Laffont', 'OL35674671M', '2006', 'Espagnol', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 445, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'An innocent man is about to be executed.\r\nOnly a guilty man can save him.\r\n \r\nIn 1998, in the small East Texas city of Sloan, Travis Boyette abducted, raped, and strangled a popular high school cheerleader. He buried her body so that it would never be found, then watched in amazement as police and prosecutors arrested and convicted Donté Drumm, a local football star, and marched him off to death row.\r\nNow nine years have passed. Travis has just been paroled in Kansas for a different crime; Donté is four days away from his execution. Travis suffers from an inoperable brain tumor. For the first time in his miserable life, he decides to do what’s right and confess. But how can a guilty man convince lawyers, judges, and politicians that they’re about to execute an innocent man?', 'An innocent man is about to be executed.\r\nOnly a guilty man can save him.\r\n \r\nIn 1998, in the small East Texas city of Sloan, Travis Boyette abducted, raped, and strangled a popular high school cheerleader. He buried her body so that it would never be found, then watched in amazement as police and prosecutors arrested and convicted Donté Drumm, a local football star, and marched him off to death row.\r\nNow nine years have passed. Travis has just been paroled in Kansas for a different crime; Donté', 0.00, 0, 0, 'nyt:mass_market_paperback=2011-07-23, New York Times bestseller, death penalty, Judicial error, Fiction, Death row inmates, Executions and executioners, Fiction, legal, Fiction, thrillers, general, Large type books, Fiction, thrillers, Suspense fiction, Legal stories, Large print books, Roman policier, Erreur judiciaire, Romans, nouvelles, Condamnés à mort, Cheerleaders, Errors', 1, '2026-07-20 23:52:04', '2026-07-20 23:52:04'),
