(151, 'a067fe65-d9e6-4b26-b3e6-f0937b50cc36', '9783453170520', 'Hannibal', NULL, 'Thomas Harris', 'Heyne Hörbuch, Mchn.', 'OL33891535M', '1999', 'Anglais', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 514, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Sequel to: [The Silence of the Lambs][1]\r\n\r\nHannibal is a novel by American author Thomas Harris, published in 1999. It is the third in his series featuring Dr. Hannibal Lecter and the second to feature FBI Special Agent Clarice Starling. The novel takes place seven years after the events of [The Silence of the Lambs](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL23481W) and deals with the intended revenge of one of Lecter\'s victims.\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://openlibrary.org/works/OL23481W/The_silence_of_the_lambs', 'Sequel to: [The Silence of the Lambs][1]\r\n\r\nHannibal is a novel by American author Thomas Harris, published in 1999. It is the third in his series featuring Dr. Hannibal Lecter and the second to feature FBI Special Agent Clarice Starling. The novel takes place seven years after the events of [The Silence of the Lambs](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL23481W) and deals with the intended revenge of one of Lecter\'s victims.\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://openlibrary.org/works/OL23481W/The_silence_of_the_lambs', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Government investigators, Revenge, Fugitives from justice, Serial murderers, Psychological fiction, Suspense fiction, horror fiction, mystery fiction, Federal Bureau of Investigation, mentally ill offenders, employees, lobotomy, prefrontal cortex, psychotropic drugs, behavioral therapy, brainwashing, sodomy, child sexual abuse, rape', 1, '2026-07-20 23:52:15', '2026-07-20 23:52:15'),
(152, '29e01461-94d5-402e-9957-5711241494ae', '9781409004431', 'Lords and Ladies', NULL, 'Terry Pratchett', 'Pocket', 'OL62086495M', '1992', 'Français', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 377, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'The fairies are back - but this time they don\'t just want your teeth...\r\n\r\nGranny Weatherwax and her tiny coven are up against real elves.\r\n\r\nIt\'s Midsummer Night.\r\n\r\nNo times for dreaming...\r\n\r\nWith full supporting cast of dwarfs, wizards, trolls, Morris dancers and one orang-utan. And lots of hey-nonny-nonny and blood all over the place.', 'The fairies are back - but this time they don\'t just want your teeth...\r\n\r\nGranny Weatherwax and her tiny coven are up against real elves.\r\n\r\nIt\'s Midsummer Night.\r\n\r\nNo times for dreaming...\r\n\r\nWith full supporting cast of dwarfs, wizards, trolls, Morris dancers and one orang-utan. And lots of hey-nonny-nonny and blood all over the place.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Discworld (Imaginary place), Fantasy, Fiction, fantasy, general, Discworld (imaginary place), fiction, Granny weatherwax (fictitious character), fiction, Drama, Fiction, humorous, Literature and fiction (general), Literature and fiction, fantasy, English Fantasy fiction, Translations into Dutch, Witches, English literature', 1, '2026-07-20 23:52:16', '2026-07-20 23:52:16'),
(153, '0b2f2f7d-dbd4-4cdd-9076-7987cb280847', '9785553863074', 'Player Piano', NULL, 'Kurt Vonnegut, Christian Rummel', 'Dell', 'OL47743826M', '1952', 'Français', 'Romans', 'technology', 'paperback', 'all', 310, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Vonnegut\'s first novel spins the chilling tale of engineer Paul Proteus, who must find a way to live in a world dominated by a super computer and run completely by machines.  Paul\'s rebellion is vintage Vonnegut - wildly funny, deadly serious, and terrifyingly close to reality.', 'Vonnegut\'s first novel spins the chilling tale of engineer Paul Proteus, who must find a way to live in a world dominated by a super computer and run completely by machines.  Paul\'s rebellion is vintage Vonnegut - wildly funny, deadly serious, and terrifyingly close to reality.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Classic Literature, Mystery, Science Fiction & Fantasy, Utopias, Computers, Science fiction, Machinery, Engineers, Long Now Manual for Civilization, American fiction (fictional works by one author)', 1, '2026-07-20 23:52:17', '2026-07-20 23:52:17'),
(154, '4ffe1668-bd71-4877-86d9-268f4e3f5f30', '9788408022503', 'Until You', NULL, 'Judith McNaught', 'Bantam', 'OL47136728M', '1994', 'rus', 'Romans', 'history', 'paperback', 'all', 432, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '(Westmoreland, #3)\r\nA teacher in a school for wealthy young ladies, Sheridan, Bromleigh is hired to accompany one of her students, heiress Charise Lancaster, to England to meet her fiancé. When her charge elopes with a stranger, Sheridan wonders how she will ever explain it to Charise\'s intended, Lord Burleton. \r\nStanding on the pier, Stephen Westmoreland, the Earl of Langford, assumes the young woman coming toward him is Charise Lancaster -- and informs her of his inadvertent role in a fatal accident involving Lord Burleton the night before. And just as Sheridan is about to speak, she steps into the path of a cargo net loaded with crates! \r\nSheridan awakens in Westmoreland\'s mansion with no memory of who she is; the only hint of her past is the puzzling fact that everyone calls her Miss Lancaster. All she truly knows is that she is falling in love with a handsome English earl, and that the life unfolding before her seems full of wondrous possibilities...\r\n\r\nWestmoreland Series: \r\nA Kingdom of Dreams (Westmoreland, #1)\r\nWhitney, My Love (Westmoreland, #2)\r\nUntil You (Westmoreland, #3)\r\nMiracles (Westmoreland, #3.5)\r\nThe following Contain \"Miracles\" (Westmoreland, #3.5):\r\nSimple Gifts: Just Curious / Miracles / Change of Heart / Double Exposure (Westmoreland, #3.5)\r\nA Holiday of Love (Westmoreland, #3.5)\r\nCharacters from the Westmoreland Dynasty Saga universe appear across the Sequels  novels. If you\'d like to read in order:\r\nA Kingdom of Dreams (Westmoreland, #1)\r\nOnce and Always (Sequels, #1)\r\nSomething Wonderful (Sequels, #2)\r\nAlmost Heaven (Sequels, #3)\r\nWhitney, My Love (Westmoreland, #2)\r\nUntil You (Westmoreland, #3)\r\nMiracles (Westmoreland, #3.5)\r\nThe following Contain \"Miracles\" (Westmoreland, #3.5):\r\nSimple Gifts: Just Curious / Miracles / Change of Heart / Double Exposure (Westmoreland, #3.5)\r\nA Holiday of Love (Westmoreland, #3.5)', '(Westmoreland, #3)\r\nA teacher in a school for wealthy young ladies, Sheridan, Bromleigh is hired to accompany one of her students, heiress Charise Lancaster, to England to meet her fiancé. When her charge elopes with a stranger, Sheridan wonders how she will ever explain it to Charise\'s intended, Lord Burleton. \r\nStanding on the pier, Stephen Westmoreland, the Earl of Langford, assumes the young woman coming toward him is Charise Lancaster -- and informs her of his inadvertent role in a fatal ac', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Romance, Historical, Americans, fiction, Amnesia,  fiction, Cuentos de amor, Estadounidenses, Ficción, Man-woman relationships, fiction, Novela histórica, Relaciones hombre-mujer, Travel, England, fiction, Large type books, Westmoreland family, fiction', 1, '2026-07-20 23:52:17', '2026-07-20 23:52:17'),
