(177, '8bbb623b-2058-4272-81f0-ab26f1450229', '9780786270880', 'Captivated', NULL, 'Nora Roberts, Therese Plummer', 'InterMix', 'OL27126107M', '1992', 'rus', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 304, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Screenwriter Nash Kirkland figured self-proclaimed witch Morgana Donovan would be a great \"resource\" for his next horror movie. The problem was, getting to know Morgana was becoming an obsession.\r\n\r\nWas he truly in love, or was he just bewitched?\r\n\r\nMorgana could accept Nash\'s skepticism, and, fortunately for him, she found him outrageously attractive as well as endearingly sweet. But could an ordinary man handle being in love with a rather extraordinary woman?\r\n\r\nDONOVAN LEGACY: Special gifts... for three magical cousins.', 'Screenwriter Nash Kirkland figured self-proclaimed witch Morgana Donovan would be a great \"resource\" for his next horror movie. The problem was, getting to know Morgana was becoming an obsession.\r\n\r\nWas he truly in love, or was he just bewitched?\r\n\r\nMorgana could accept Nash\'s skepticism, and, fortunately for him, she found him outrageously attractive as well as endearingly sweet. But could an ordinary man handle being in love with a rather extraordinary woman?\r\n\r\nDONOVAN LEGACY: Special gifts..', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Open Library Staff Picks, Donovan Legacy, Screenwriters, Fiction, Romance, Fantasy, 1990s, Psychics, Contemporary, Love stories, American, Large type books, Donovan family (Fictitious characters), Fiction, romance, general, Donovan family (fictitious characters), fiction, Fiction, romance, contemporary, Witches', 1, '2026-07-20 23:52:44', '2026-07-20 23:52:44'),
(178, '33bd5e58-c86f-408d-9d5a-e9a5b8363746', '9781860462979', 'Ensaio Sobre a Cegueira', NULL, 'José Saramago', 'Harvill Press', 'OL61412784M', '1995', 'Allemand', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 352, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Uma cegueira branca se espalha de forma fulminante. Internados em quarentena ou perdidos pela cidade, os cegos devem enfrentar o que há de mais primitivo na espécie humana: a vontade de sobreviver à qualquer custo.\r\n\r\nJosé Saramago, vencedor do Prêmio Nobel de Literatura de 1998, tece uma aterrorizante parábola sobre o ser humano, que revela o que há de pior em nós mesmos.', 'Uma cegueira branca se espalha de forma fulminante. Internados em quarentena ou perdidos pela cidade, os cegos devem enfrentar o que há de mais primitivo na espécie humana: a vontade de sobreviver à qualquer custo.\r\n\r\nJosé Saramago, vencedor do Prêmio Nobel de Literatura de 1998, tece uma aterrorizante parábola sobre o ser humano, que revela o que há de pior em nós mesmos.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Blind, Blindness, Fiction, Modern Literature, Allegories, Psychological fiction, Psychology, Epidemics, Survival, Blind in literature, Violence, Large type books, Novela, Portugal, Dystopian, Literary Fiction, Disease Outbreaks', 1, '2026-07-20 23:52:46', '2026-07-20 23:52:46'),
