(200, 'af63e25e-067d-4edf-9529-91bc44a3826e', '9780374722104', 'Find Me', NULL, 'André Aciman', 'Faber & Faber, Limited', 'OL47701611M', '2019', 'Anglais', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 266, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'In the beginning, we are shown Elio\'s father, Samuel, on a trip from Florence to Rome to visit Elio, who has become a gifted classical pianist. A chance encounter on the train with a beautiful young woman named Miranda, she upended Samuels plans and changes his life forever.', 'In the beginning, we are shown Elio\'s father, Samuel, on a trip from Florence to Rome to visit Elio, who has become a gifted classical pianist. A chance encounter on the train with a beautiful young woman named Miranda, she upended Samuels plans and changes his life forever.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'nyt:combined-print-and-e-book-fiction=2019-11-17, New York Times bestseller, New York Times reviewed, Fiction, gay, Gay men, fiction, Musicians, fiction, Gay men, Fiction, FICTION / Literary, FICTION / LGBT / Gay, Homosexuels masculins, Romans, nouvelles, Homosexualité masculine, Souvenir, Pianistes, Pères et fils', 1, '2026-07-20 23:53:10', '2026-07-20 23:53:10'),
