(239, '87462b3a-0cb0-4638-8c6f-5b0c0a348962', '9788845212178', 'The Stand', NULL, 'Stephen King', 'Knopf Doubleday Publishing Group', 'OL61439825M', '1978', 'Italien', 'Romans', 'science', 'paperback', 'all', 1153, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'One man escapes from a biological weapon facility after an accident, carrying with him the deadly virus known as Captain Tripps, a rapidly mutating flu that - in the ensuing weeks - wipes out most of the world\'s population. In the aftermath, survivors choose between following an elderly black woman to Boulder or the dark man, Randall Flagg, who has set up his command post in Las Vegas. The two factions prepare for a confrontation between the forces of good and evil.\r\n([source][1])\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://stephenking.com/library/novel/stand_the.html', 'One man escapes from a biological weapon facility after an accident, carrying with him the deadly virus known as Captain Tripps, a rapidly mutating flu that - in the ensuing weeks - wipes out most of the world\'s population. In the aftermath, survivors choose between following an elderly black woman to Boulder or the dark man, Randall Flagg, who has set up his command post in Las Vegas. The two factions prepare for a confrontation between the forces of good and evil.\r\n([source][1])\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: ht', 0.00, 0, 0, 'suspense & thriller, gothic & horror, biological warfare, research, horror fiction, horror tales, Fiction, Thrillers, Suspense, Horror, Science Fiction, Apocalyptic & Post-Apocalyptic science fiction, nuclear weapons, cordon sanitaire, index cases, martial law, post-apocalyptic, influenza, pandemic, End of the World', 1, '2026-07-20 23:54:02', '2026-07-20 23:54:02'),
(240, 'cf003c45-44c2-4e6a-ac8e-24945c33fc6c', '9780671606848', 'Flowers in the Attic', NULL, 'V.C. Andrews', 'Piatkus', 'OL51481730M', '1979', 'pol', 'Romans', 'children', 'paperback', 'children', 411, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Flowers in the Attic is a 1979 Gothic novel by V. C. Andrews. It is the first book in the Dollanganger Series. The novel is written in the first-person, from the point of view of Cathy Dollanganger. In 1993, Flowers in the Attic was awarded the Secondary BILBY Award. In 2003 the book was listed on the BBC\'s The Big Read poll of the UK\'s 200 \"best-loved novels.\"\r\n\r\n\r\n----------\r\nAlso contained in:\r\n[Flowers in the Attic / Petals on the Wind](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16524231W)', 'Flowers in the Attic is a 1979 Gothic novel by V. C. Andrews. It is the first book in the Dollanganger Series. The novel is written in the first-person, from the point of view of Cathy Dollanganger. In 1993, Flowers in the Attic was awarded the Secondary BILBY Award. In 2003 the book was listed on the BBC\'s The Big Read poll of the UK\'s 200 \"best-loved novels.\"\r\n\r\n\r\n----------\r\nAlso contained in:\r\n[Flowers in the Attic / Petals on the Wind](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16524231W)', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Gothic fiction, Psychological Thriller, coming of age, classics, series:dollanganger, doughnuts, incest, Psychological fiction, Fiction, abused children, brothers and sisters, grandparents, child abuse, Novela, Hermanos, Ficcion, Abuso de niños, Niños maltratados, Abuelos, American fiction', 1, '2026-07-20 23:54:05', '2026-07-20 23:54:05'),
(241, 'a1b731b9-69b4-473d-ac2e-45ce30567f20', '9781101192740', 'Desperation', NULL, 'Stephen King', 'Hodder & Stoughton Ltd', 'OL53243209M', '1996', 'Italien', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 616, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Located off a desolate stretch of Interstate 50, Desperation, Nevada has few connections with the rest of the world. It is a place, though, where the seams between worlds are thin. Miners at the China Pit have accidentally broken into another dimension and released a horrific creature known as Tak, who takes human form by hijacking some of the town\'s residents. The forces of good orchestrate a confrontation between this ancient evil and a group of unsuspecting travelers who are lured to the dying town. This rag-tag band of unwilling champions is led by a young boy who speaks to God. \r\n\r\n([source][1])\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://www.stephenking.com/library/novel/desperation.html', 'Located off a desolate stretch of Interstate 50, Desperation, Nevada has few connections with the rest of the world. It is a place, though, where the seams between worlds are thin. Miners at the China Pit have accidentally broken into another dimension and released a horrific creature known as Tak, who takes human form by hijacking some of the town\'s residents. The forces of good orchestrate a confrontation between this ancient evil and a group of unsuspecting travelers who are lured to the dyin', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Travelers, Traffic police, American fiction, Horror tales, Horror, Suspense, Psychological fiction, Spanish: Adult Fiction, Horror fiction, Police, American Horror tales, American literature, Large type books, Fiction, horror, Nevada, fiction, Spanish language, Novela estadounidense, Novela fantástica, Novela psicológica', 1, '2026-07-20 23:54:05', '2026-07-20 23:54:05'),
(242, '51893c48-9722-4daa-91e6-e9420f403f0d', '9780736649254', 'Libra', NULL, 'Don DeLillo', 'Izd-vo \"ĖKSMO\"', 'OL47384997M', '1988', 'rus', 'Romans', 'history', 'paperback', 'all', 468, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'In this powerful, eerily convincing fictional speculation on the assassination of John F. Kennedy, Don DeLillo chronicles Lee Harvey Oswald\'s odyssey from troubled teenager to a man of precarious stability who imagines himself an agent of history. When \"history\" presents itself in the form of two disgruntled CIA operatives who decide that an unsuccessful attempt on the life of the president will galvanize the nation against communism, the scales are irrevocably tipped. A gripping, masterful blend of fact and fiction, alive with meticulously portrayed characters both real and created, Libra is a grave, haunting, and brilliant examination of an event that has become an indelible part of the American psyche.', 'In this powerful, eerily convincing fictional speculation on the assassination of John F. Kennedy, Don DeLillo chronicles Lee Harvey Oswald\'s odyssey from troubled teenager to a man of precarious stability who imagines himself an agent of history. When \"history\" presents itself in the form of two disgruntled CIA operatives who decide that an unsuccessful attempt on the life of the president will galvanize the nation against communism, the scales are irrevocably tipped. A gripping, masterful blen', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Assassination, Assassins, Presidents, Literature, Roman américain, Présidents, Assassinat, Romans, nouvelles, Fiction, historical, Presidents, united states, fiction, Fiction, fantasy, historical, Large type books, American fiction (fictional works by one author), Oswald, lee harvey, Assassinationkennedy, john f. (john fitzgerald) , 1917-1963, Ps3554.e4425 l53 2006, Roman, Fiction, general, American literature', 1, '2026-07-20 23:54:06', '2026-07-20 23:54:06'),
(243, '60f7194e-9df8-4c79-b584-9fae1734599e', '9782290155066', 'The Colorado Kid', NULL, 'Stephen King', 'DEBOLSILLO', 'OL60775605M', '1978', 'Anglais', 'Romans', 'science', 'paperback', 'all', 184, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'The Colorado Kid is a mystery novel by American writer Stephen King, published by the Hard Case Crime imprint in 2005. The book was initially issued in one paperback-only edition by the specialty crime and mystery publishing house. Hard Case Crime reissued The Colorado Kid in an illustrated paperback edition in May 2019.', 'The Colorado Kid is a mystery novel by American writer Stephen King, published by the Hard Case Crime imprint in 2005. The book was initially issued in one paperback-only edition by the specialty crime and mystery publishing house. Hard Case Crime reissued The Colorado Kid in an illustrated paperback edition in May 2019.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Crime Mysteries, Forensic sciences, Fiction, Homicide investigation, Investigation, Newspaper employees, Missing persons, Mystery fiction, American literature, Identification, Islands, Homicide investigation -- Maine -- Fiction., Missing persons -- Investigation -- Maine -- Fiction., Newspaper employees -- Fiction., Forensic sciences -- Fiction., Maine -- Fiction.', 1, '2026-07-20 23:54:07', '2026-07-20 23:54:07'),
(244, '44160fdb-c575-4a1b-9451-004c5b0045aa', '9781551662312', 'Power Play (Mills and Boon Despatch Cycle)', NULL, 'Penny Jordan', 'Harlequin', 'OL21331027M', '1988', 'Anglais', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 509, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Ten years ago, Rachel Lee was a poor gypsy girl, who with great effort managed to go to the University. There she met an attractive and privileged young boy, but he and three friends raped her, destroying her illusions.\r\n \r\nNow, she is Pepper Minesse, and she is out to destroy the lives of the four men. Finally, she has the edge - enough evidence to blackmail them and ruin their very successful, very public lives. But they have plans of their own, plans to protect their secrets at all costs, and Pepper must suddenly rely on an unexpected ally to save herself. He was Miles French, one of the men involved in the attack.', 'Ten years ago, Rachel Lee was a poor gypsy girl, who with great effort managed to go to the University. There she met an attractive and privileged young boy, but he and three friends raped her, destroying her illusions.\r\n \r\nNow, she is Pepper Minesse, and she is out to destroy the lives of the four men. Finally, she has the edge - enough evidence to blackmail them and ruin their very successful, very public lives. But they have plans of their own, plans to protect their secrets at all costs, and', 0.00, 0, 0, 'England, fiction, London (england), fiction, Fiction, romance, general, Fiction, romance, contemporary, Revenge, Fiction, Fiction, romance, suspense', 1, '2026-07-20 23:54:09', '2026-07-20 23:54:09'),
