(431, '8b10f309-5d3d-447c-9cb1-10bd119d1117', '9781441622372', 'A Confederacy of Dunces', NULL, 'John Kennedy Toole', 'Dtv', 'OL47067884M', '1980', 'Espagnol', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 391, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'A Confederacy of Dunces is an American comic masterpiece. John Kennedy Toole\'s hero is one Ignatius J. Reilly, \"huge, obese, fractious, fastidious, a latter-day Gargantua, a Don Quixote of the French Quarter. His story bursts with wholly original characters, denizens of New Orleans\' lower depths, incredibly true-to-life dialogue, and the zaniest series of high and low comic adventures.\"', 'A Confederacy of Dunces is an American comic masterpiece. John Kennedy Toole\'s hero is one Ignatius J. Reilly, \"huge, obese, fractious, fastidious, a latter-day Gargantua, a Don Quixote of the French Quarter. His story bursts with wholly original characters, denizens of New Orleans\' lower depths, incredibly true-to-life dialogue, and the zaniest series of high and low comic adventures.\"', 0.00, 0, 0, 'mothers, travel, housing, character, sons, groups, loneliness, Young men, Mothers and sons, Fiction, Long Now Manual for Civilization, Reading Level-Grade 7, Reading Level-Grade 9, Reading Level-Grade 8, Reading Level-Grade 11, Reading Level-Grade 10, Reading Level-Grade 12, Fiction, humorous, Mothers and sons, fiction, New orleans (la.), fiction', 1, '2026-07-20 23:58:04', '2026-07-20 23:58:04'),
