(790, '76a5d034-7c99-4976-8e21-c45827a30775', '9780312304355', 'Moloka\'i', NULL, 'Alan Brennert', 'St. Martin\'s Griffin', 'OL35353090M', '2003', 'Anglais', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 395, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Hawaï, 1892. Rachel Kalama, jeune fille de sept ans à l\'esprit vif et malicieux, rêve de visiter des contrées lointaines comme son père, un officier de la marine marchande. Jusqu\'au jour où une tache rosâtre apparaît sur sa peau et que ses rêves s\'envolent. Atteinte de la lèpre, la petite Rachel est arrachée à son foyer et à sa famille, et envoyée à Kalaupapa, campement de quarantaine installé sur l\'île de Moloka\'i où elle sera confinée jusqu\'à l\'âge adulte. Entourée de malades, Rachel devra se forger une existence, bien différente de celle qu\'elle avait prévue. La résilience et l\'entraide l\'aideront à surmonter le déracinement, l\'ostracisme et la perte. Débordant de chaleur, d\'humour, de compassion, et fort d\'une galerie de personnages inoubliables, ce chef-d\'oeuvre nous dévoile un peuple qui, face à la terrible réalité de la mort, a choisi la vie.--[Memento].', 'Hawaï, 1892. Rachel Kalama, jeune fille de sept ans à l\'esprit vif et malicieux, rêve de visiter des contrées lointaines comme son père, un officier de la marine marchande. Jusqu\'au jour où une tache rosâtre apparaît sur sa peau et que ses rêves s\'envolent. Atteinte de la lèpre, la petite Rachel est arrachée à son foyer et à sa famille, et envoyée à Kalaupapa, campement de quarantaine installé sur l\'île de Moloka\'i où elle sera confinée jusqu\'à l\'âge adulte. Entourée de malades, Rachel devra se', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Leprosy in fiction, Patients, Women, Leprosy, Women in fiction, Fiction, general, Hawaii, fiction, Fiction, psychological, Fiction, medical, Psychological fiction', 1, '2026-07-21 00:05:26', '2026-07-21 00:05:26'),
(791, '5bb9c61c-613b-4146-a2fa-b51cc17f954a', '9780385363259', 'First Sight', NULL, 'Danielle Steel', 'PC Domaine Etranger', 'OL43689575M', '2006', 'rus', 'Romans', 'history', 'paperback', 'all', 476, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'New York. London. Milan. Paris. Fashion Week in all four cities. A month of endless interviews, parties, and unflagging work and attention to detail at the ready to wear fashion shows twice a year. At the center of the storm is American Timmie O\'Neill, whose renowned line, Timmie O, is the embodiment of casual chic in fashion and for the home. She has created a business that inspires, fills, and consumes her life. With an unerring instinct for what the next trend will be, Timmie has built an international empire over two decades that has brought her enormous satisfaction and success. Yet as blessed as she feels, Timmie harbors the wounds of a devastating childhood and past tragedy. She is too hurt to want much in her personal life beyond a succession of very limited relationships. Always willing to take risks in business, she never risks her heart. But despite her highly controlled world, Timmie O\'Neill is not immune to magic when it strikes. And it strikes during Paris Fashion Week, when an intriguing Frenchman comes into her life. At first, Timmie and Jean-Charles Vernier are only patient and physicians, but neither can deny their growing friendship and the electricity that sparks whenever they meet.', 'New York. London. Milan. Paris. Fashion Week in all four cities. A month of endless interviews, parties, and unflagging work and attention to detail at the ready to wear fashion shows twice a year. At the center of the storm is American Timmie O\'Neill, whose renowned line, Timmie O, is the embodiment of casual chic in fashion and for the home. She has created a business that inspires, fills, and consumes her life. With an unerring instinct for what the next trend will be, Timmie has built an int', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Clothing trade, Fashion, Fiction, Women executives, Clothing and dress, Amerikanisches Englisch, Clothing industry, nyt:hardcover-fiction=2013-08-04, New York Times bestseller, Women-owned business enterprises, Man-woman relationships, Adultery, Orphans, Women fashion designers, Fiction, romance, contemporary, Fiction, women, Paris (france), fiction, Love stories, nyt:mass-market-paperback=2014-05-18, Large type books', 1, '2026-07-21 00:05:27', '2026-07-21 00:05:27'),
(792, '2cc1e28f-7766-48b5-8697-713eab6fca7a', '9783453271845', 'The Outsider', NULL, 'Stephen King', 'Altn Kitaplar', 'OL61027675M', '2018', 'Espagnol', 'Romans', 'children', 'paperback', 'children', 582, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '\"An unspeakable crime. A confounding investigation. At a time when the King brand has never been stronger, he has delivered one of his most unsettling and compulsively readable stories. An eleven-year-old boy\'s violated corpse is found in a town park. Eyewitnesses and fingerprints point unmistakably to one of Flint City\'s most popular citizens. He is Terry Maitland, Little League coach, English teacher, husband, and father of two girls. Detective Ralph Anderson, whose son Maitland once coached, orders a quick and very public arrest. Maitland has an alibi, but Anderson and the district attorney soon add DNA evidence to go with the fingerprints and witnesses. Their case seems ironclad. As the investigation expands and horrifying answers begin to emerge, King\'s propulsive story kicks into high gear, generating strong tension and almost unbearable suspense. Terry Maitland seems like a nice guy, but is he wearing another face? When the answer comes, it will shock you as only Stephen King can.\"--\r\n\r\nAn eleven-year-old boy\'s violated corpse is found in a town park. Eyewitnesses and fingerprints point unmistakably to one of Flint City\'s most popular citizens:  Terry Maitland, Little League coach, English teacher, husband, and father of two girls. Detective Ralph Anderson orders a quick and very public arrest. The case seems ironclad, especially when Anderson and the district attorney are able to add DNA evidence to go with the fingerprints and witnesses. But Maitland has an alibi, and it turns out his story has incontrovertible evidence of its own. How can two opposing stories be true? -- adapted from publisher info', '\"An unspeakable crime. A confounding investigation. At a time when the King brand has never been stronger, he has delivered one of his most unsettling and compulsively readable stories. An eleven-year-old boy\'s violated corpse is found in a town park. Eyewitnesses and fingerprints point unmistakably to one of Flint City\'s most popular citizens. He is Terry Maitland, Little League coach, English teacher, husband, and father of two girls. Detective Ralph Anderson, whose son Maitland once coached,', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Murder, Rape victims, Alibi, Fiction, Shapeshifters, Criminal Evidence, Investigation, Large type books, Fiction, horror, Fiction, thrillers, Fiction, thrillers, general, nyt:combined-print-and-e-book-fiction=2018-06-10, New York Times bestseller, New York Times reviewed, Psychological Horror, Horror, Thriller, Mystery, Crime, Mystery Thriller', 1, '2026-07-21 00:05:27', '2026-07-21 00:05:27'),
(793, '0a321185-e2e2-471a-a9a0-d58c440a802d', '9788535931327', 'Giovanni\'s Room', NULL, 'James Baldwin', 'Penguin Books, Limited', 'OL36681450M', '1956', 'Français', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 224, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Considered an \'audacious\' second novel, GIOVANNI\'S ROOM is set in the 1950s Paris of American expatriates, liaisons, and violence.  This now-classic story of a fated love triangle explores, with uncompromising clarity, the conflicts between desire, conventional morality and sexual identity.', 'Considered an \'audacious\' second novel, GIOVANNI\'S ROOM is set in the 1950s Paris of American expatriates, liaisons, and violence.  This now-classic story of a fated love triangle explores, with uncompromising clarity, the conflicts between desire, conventional morality and sexual identity.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Race relations, African Americans, Psychology, Afro-Americans, Giovanni, Nikki, Fiction, Americans in fiction, Americans, Sexual behavior, Homosexuality in fiction, Sexual orientation, Men, Bisexuals in fiction, Men in fiction, Sexual orientation in fiction, Homosexuality, Bisexuals, Classic Literature, Gay men, Fiction, african american, general', 1, '2026-07-21 00:05:30', '2026-07-21 00:05:30'),
