(837, '1dea38f1-c35e-49c6-a818-1f758c3274fd', '9780446402231', 'The gold coast', NULL, 'Nelson DeMille', 'Pocket', 'OL58234025M', '1990', 'heb', 'Romans', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 626, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Welcome to the fabled Gold Coast, that stretch on the North Shore of Long Island that once held the greatest concentration of wealth and power in America. Here two men are destined for an explosive collision: John Sutter, Wall Street lawyer, holding fast to a fading aristocratic legacy; and Frank Bellarosa, the Mafia don who seizes his piece of the staid and unprepared Gold Coast like a latter-day barbarian chief and draws Sutter and his regally beautiful wife, Susan, into his violent world. Told from Sutter\'s sardonic and often hilarious point of view, and laced with sexual passion and suspense, The Gold Coast is Nelson DeMille\'s captivating story of friendship and seduction, love and betrayal.', 'Welcome to the fabled Gold Coast, that stretch on the North Shore of Long Island that once held the greatest concentration of wealth and power in America. Here two men are destined for an explosive collision: John Sutter, Wall Street lawyer, holding fast to a fading aristocratic legacy; and Frank Bellarosa, the Mafia don who seizes his piece of the staid and unprepared Gold Coast like a latter-day barbarian chief and draws Sutter and his regally beautiful wife, Susan, into his violent world. Tol', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, thrillers, espionage, New jersey, fiction, Fiction, mystery & detective, general, Fiction, La vie et coutumes sociales, Social life and customs, Mystery, Detective and mystery stories, Manners and customs, Mafia, Large type books, Fiction, general, nyt:mass-market-paperback=2008-11-16, New York Times bestseller, Legal stories, Revenge, Romans, nouvelles, Mœurs et coutumes, Fiction, thrillers, general, Fiction, thrillers, suspense', 1, '2026-07-21 00:06:26', '2026-07-21 00:06:26'),
(838, 'e6d2bc8e-9bb9-449e-ba2c-2523a0d18492', '9780440242000', 'Bleachers', NULL, 'John Grisham', NULL, 'OL24101709M', '2003', 'pol', 'Romans', 'school', 'paperback', 'all', 190, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Bij het sterfbed van zijn coach maakt de voormalige sterspeler van een American football team de balans op van zijn jeugd.', 'Bij het sterfbed van zijn coach maakt de voormalige sterspeler van een American football team de balans op van zijn jeugd.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Death, Teacher-student relationships, Funeral rites and ceremonies, School sports, Football players, Football coaches, Fiction, Fiction, sports, Ritos y ceremonias fúnebres, Novela, Relaciones maestro-estudiante, Fútbol americano, Muerte, Football stories, American Psychological fiction, Translations into Spanish, Novela psicología, Texas, fiction, Fiction, psychological', 1, '2026-07-21 00:06:28', '2026-07-21 00:06:28'),
(839, '36108888-eca4-48f8-a5c8-566cdb830649', '9785739007513', 'Двенадцать стульев', NULL, 'Илья Арнольдович Ильф, Евгений Петрович Петров', 'Northwestern University Press', 'OL22341609M', '1938', 'Français', 'Romans', 'history', 'paperback', 'all', 395, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '\"Ostap Bender is an unemployed con artist living by his wits in postrevolutionary Soviet Russia. He joins forces with Ippolit Matveyevich Vorobyaninov, a former nobleman who has returned to his hometown to find a cache of missing jewels which were hidden in some chairs that have been appropriated by the Soviet authorities.\r\n\r\nThe search for the bejeweled chairs takes these unlikely heroes from the provinces to Moscow to the wilds of Soviet Georgia and the Trans-caucasus mountains; on their quest they encounter a wide variety of characters: from opportunistic Soviet bureaucrats to aging survivors of the prerevolutionary propertied classes, each one more selfish, venal, and ineffective than the one before.\"--BOOK JACKET.', '\"Ostap Bender is an unemployed con artist living by his wits in postrevolutionary Soviet Russia. He joins forces with Ippolit Matveyevich Vorobyaninov, a former nobleman who has returned to his hometown to find a cache of missing jewels which were hidden in some chairs that have been appropriated by the Soviet authorities.\r\n\r\nThe search for the bejeweled chairs takes these unlikely heroes from the provinces to Moscow to the wilds of Soviet Georgia and the Trans-caucasus mountains; on their quest', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Continental european fiction (fictional works by one author), Ficiton, Description and travel, Lost articles, Russian fiction, Satire, Fiction, humorous, general, Social life and customs, History, Swindlers and swindling, Jewelry, Lost articles--fiction, Russian fiction--20th century, Lost articles--ficiton, Pg3476.i44 d913 2011, 891.73/42', 1, '2026-07-21 00:06:28', '2026-07-21 00:06:28'),
