(870, 'db0cdc4a-5d0e-4e85-84da-859a18bfd32a', '9780140287363', 'Das Ende einer Affäre', NULL, 'Graham Greene, Eduardo Jordá, Monica Ali', 'Shi bao wen hua chu ban gong si', 'OL60329052M', '1951', 'hun', 'Romans', 'history', 'paperback', 'all', 237, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'The story of an obsessive love affair between a married woman and a young up-and-coming writer. Almost as soon as he begins the affair the writer realizes it cannot last though he still cannot stop himself from becoming jealous of the woman’s husband and cannot bring himself to end it.', 'The story of an obsessive love affair between a married woman and a young up-and-coming writer. Almost as soon as he begins the affair the writer realizes it cannot last though he still cannot stop himself from becoming jealous of the woman’s husband and cannot bring himself to end it.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Schriftsteller, Belletristische Darstellung, Dreierbeziehung, Male friendship, World War, 1939-1945, Open Library Staff Picks, Fiction in English, Terminally ill, Fiction, Loss (Psychology), Triangles (Interpersonal relations), Adultery, Triangles (Interpersonal relations) -- Fiction, Religious fiction, Psychological fiction, Love stories, Fiction, romance, general, Friendship, fiction, London (england), fiction, British and irish fiction (fictional works by one author)', 1, '2026-07-21 00:07:06', '2026-07-21 00:07:06'),
(871, 'b84c26de-a9b0-48d5-8950-d9cf9007167d', '9789754709612', 'Snow', NULL, 'Orhan Pamuk', 'ALFAGUARA', 'OL44279966M', '2002', 'hin', 'Romans', 'magazine', 'paperback', 'all', 496, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Touching, slyly comic, and humming with cerebral suspense—a masterful novel of \"political intrigue and philosophy, romance and noir\" (Vogue) and the lethal chemistry between secular doubt and Islamic fanaticism from the Nobel Prize winner.\r\n\r\nAn exiled poet named Ka returns to Turkey and travels to the forlorn city of Kars. His ostensible purpose is to report on a wave of suicides among religious girls forbidden to wear their head-scarves. But Ka is also drawn by his memories of the radiant Ipek, now recently divorced.\r\n\r\nAmid blanketing snowfall and universal suspicion, Ka finds himself pursued by figures ranging from Ipek’s ex-husband to a charismatic terrorist. A lost gift returns with ecstatic suddenness. A theatrical evening climaxes in a massacre. And finding god may be the prelude to losing everything else.', 'Touching, slyly comic, and humming with cerebral suspense—a masterful novel of \"political intrigue and philosophy, romance and noir\" (Vogue) and the lethal chemistry between secular doubt and Islamic fanaticism from the Nobel Prize winner.\r\n\r\nAn exiled poet named Ka returns to Turkey and travels to the forlorn city of Kars. His ostensible purpose is to report on a wave of suicides among religious girls forbidden to wear their head-scarves. But Ka is also drawn by his memories of the radiant Ipek', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Social conditions, Journalists, Fiction, Exiles, Condiciones sociales, Islam and politics, Islamic fundamentalism, Authors, Turkish, Turkish Poets, Exiliados, Ficción, Autores turcos, Poets, Turkish, Turkish Authors, Turkish literature, Hijab (Islamic clothing), Traducciones al espanol, Novela, Novela turca, Literature', 1, '2026-07-21 00:07:07', '2026-07-21 00:07:07'),
