(1390, '8850b953-ff0e-43e0-8212-f4b8c24467ec', '9788886845038', 'Coffey on the Mile', NULL, 'Stephen King', 'Bt Bound', 'OL50984911M', '1996', 'tur', 'Stephen King', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 138, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '[The Green Mile](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL81629W/The_Green_Mile)  #6\r\nThe final chapter in this six-part novel tells us of John Coffey\'s fate.  The story also brings us to the present day story of Paul Edgecombe and learn of the consequences of his actions during his time on E Block with John Coffey.\r\n\r\n\r\n([source][1])\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://www.stephenking.com/library/novel/green_mile_coffey_on_the_mile_the.html', '[The Green Mile](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL81629W/The_Green_Mile)  #6\r\nThe final chapter in this six-part novel tells us of John Coffey\'s fate.  The story also brings us to the present day story of Paul Edgecombe and learn of the consequences of his actions during his time on E Block with John Coffey.\r\n\r\n\r\n([source][1])\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://www.stephenking.com/library/novel/green_mile_coffey_on_the_mile_the.html', 0.00, 0, 0, 'serialized fiction, horror fiction, adventure fiction, suspense fiction, death row inmates, prison, American horror tales, Prisoners, Fiction, Prisons, Georgia, fiction, Coffey, john (fictitious character), fiction, Fiction, horror', 1, '2026-07-21 15:01:50', '2026-07-21 15:01:50'),
(1391, '4b5f3379-5466-465a-a0e6-157af190a0d7', '9782226220592', 'Under the Dome [2/2]', NULL, 'Stephen King', 'Pocket Books', 'OL28422729M', '2011', 'Français', 'Stephen King', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 585, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'All hell has broken loose in Chester\'s Mill after an invisible force field suddenly and inexplicably descends on the small Maine town, isolating all within it from the outside world. As the grim reality of the situation dawns and panic sets in, each other town\'s denizens reveals their true nature in the face of shortages, rationing, lawlessness, and uncertainty.\r\n\r\nTheir survival depends on Dale \"Barbie\" Barbara, an ex-army drifter who leads a few intrepid citizens in a race to uncover the sinister forces intent on holding the town hostage under the dome - and to raise it before there\'s on one left alive in Chester\'s Mill...\r\n\r\n\r\n----------\r\nAlso contained in:\r\n\r\n - [Under the Dome][1]\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14917748W', 'All hell has broken loose in Chester\'s Mill after an invisible force field suddenly and inexplicably descends on the small Maine town, isolating all within it from the outside world. As the grim reality of the situation dawns and panic sets in, each other town\'s denizens reveals their true nature in the face of shortages, rationing, lawlessness, and uncertainty.\r\n\r\nTheir survival depends on Dale \"Barbie\" Barbara, an ex-army drifter who leads a few intrepid citizens in a race to uncover the sinis', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Veterans, City and town life, Good and evil, Psychological fiction, Thrillers, Fantasy fiction, Suspense fiction, Fiction, suspense, Fiction, psychological, Maine, fiction, nyt:mass-market-paperback=2014-04-13, New York Times bestseller', 1, '2026-07-21 15:01:53', '2026-07-21 15:01:53'),
