(1484, 'ede0d97f-48f2-4158-98ab-4cb5811ab4e3', '9783125615557', 'The Jaunt', NULL, 'Stephen King', 'PONS', 'OL27942762M', '2009', 'Anglais', 'Stephen King', 'other', 'paperback', 'all', NULL, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '\"The Jaunt\" is a horror short story by Stephen King first published in The Twilight Zone Magazine in 1981, and collected in King\'s 1985 collection Skeleton Crew.\r\n\r\nThe story takes place early in the 24th century, when the technology for teleportation, referred to as \"Jaunting\", is commonplace, allowing for instantaneous transportation across enormous distances, even to other planets in the Solar System.\r\n\r\n\r\n----------\r\nAlso contained in:\r\n\r\n - [Skeleton Crew](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL149161W/Skeleton_Crew)', '\"The Jaunt\" is a horror short story by Stephen King first published in The Twilight Zone Magazine in 1981, and collected in King\'s 1985 collection Skeleton Crew.\r\n\r\nThe story takes place early in the 24th century, when the technology for teleportation, referred to as \"Jaunting\", is commonplace, allowing for instantaneous transportation across enormous distances, even to other planets in the Solar System.\r\n\r\n\r\n----------\r\nAlso contained in:\r\n\r\n - [Skeleton Crew](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Horror short story, teleportation, Texaco, anaesthesia, heart attack', 1, '2026-07-21 15:04:42', '2026-07-21 15:04:42'),
