(1758, 'b852d20f-e736-42e4-8564-13d05c40936b', '9780708911518', 'Cards on the Table', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'Agatha Christie Ltd', 'OL61510163M', '1936', 'Allemand', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 226, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'It was the match-up of the century: four sleuths--Superintendent Battle of Scotland Yard; Mrs. Ariadne Oliver, famed writer of detective stories; Col. Race of His Majesty\'s Secret Service; and the incomparable Hercule Poirot - invited to play bridge with four specially invited guests, each of whom had gotten away with murder! But before the first rubber was completed, the host was dead.', 'It was the match-up of the century: four sleuths--Superintendent Battle of Scotland Yard; Mrs. Ariadne Oliver, famed writer of detective stories; Col. Race of His Majesty\'s Secret Service; and the incomparable Hercule Poirot - invited to play bridge with four specially invited guests, each of whom had gotten away with murder! But before the first rubber was completed, the host was dead.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Hercule Poirot (Fictitious character), Private investigators, Private investigators in fiction, Detective and mystery stories, Mystery, Poirot, Hercule (Fictitious character) Fiction, Zhen tan xiao shuo, Chang pian xiao shuo, Fiction, mystery & detective, general, Private investigators, fiction, Large type books, English literature, Fiction, mystery & detective, traditional, England, fiction, Poirot, hercule (fictitious character), fiction, Battle, superintendent (fictitious character), fiction, Oliver, ariadne (fictitious character), fiction, Race, colonel johnny (fictitious character), fiction, Marple, jane (fictitious character), fiction', 1, '2026-07-21 15:13:34', '2026-07-21 15:13:34'),
(1759, '760c44e6-1215-4a4f-8d8a-b8864fecacad', '9781719276023', 'A Caribbean Mystery', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'Distributed by Workman Pub. Co.', 'OL55140981M', '1964', 'pol', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 224, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'As Miss Marple sat basking in the Caribbean sunshine, she felt mildly discontented with life. True, the warmth eased her rheumatism, but here in paradise nothing ever happened. Eventually, her interest was aroused by an old soldier\'s yarn about strange coincidence. Infuriatingly, just as he was about to show her an astonishing photograph, the Major\'s attention wandered. He never did finish the story...', 'As Miss Marple sat basking in the Caribbean sunshine, she felt mildly discontented with life. True, the warmth eased her rheumatism, but here in paradise nothing ever happened. Eventually, her interest was aroused by an old soldier\'s yarn about strange coincidence. Infuriatingly, just as he was about to show her an astonishing photograph, the Major\'s attention wandered. He never did finish the story...', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Agatha Christie, Miss Marple, Series, British, Amateur, Detective, Fiction, Classic, Literature, Braille, Audiobook, Crime, Murder, Mystery, Suspense, Humour, Travel, Vacation, Cruise, Caribbean', 1, '2026-07-21 15:13:36', '2026-07-21 15:13:36'),
(1760, '4c9628d6-068b-4848-aff0-93e216357f5c', '9782253242550', 'Murder in Mesopotamia', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'fontana books', 'OL58633712M', '1936', 'Français', 'Agatha Christie', 'comic', 'paperback', 'all', 248, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Nurse Amy Leatheran had never felt the lure of the ‘mysterious East,’ but she nonetheless accepts an assignment at Hassanieh, an ancient site deep in the Iraqi desert, to care for the wife of a celebrated archaeologist. Mrs Leidner is suffering bizarre visions and nervous terror. ‘I’m afraid of being killed!’ she admits to her nurse. Her terror, unfortunately, is anything but unfounded, and Nurse Leatheran is soon enough without a patient. The world’s greatest detective happens to be in the vicinity, however: having concluded an assignment in Syria, and curious about the dig at Hassanieh, Hercule Poirot arrives in time to lead a murder investigation that will tax even his remarkable powers -- and in a part of the world that has seen more than its share of misadventure and foul play.', 'Nurse Amy Leatheran had never felt the lure of the ‘mysterious East,’ but she nonetheless accepts an assignment at Hassanieh, an ancient site deep in the Iraqi desert, to care for the wife of a celebrated archaeologist. Mrs Leidner is suffering bizarre visions and nervous terror. ‘I’m afraid of being killed!’ she admits to her nurse. Her terror, unfortunately, is anything but unfounded, and Nurse Leatheran is soon enough without a patient. The world’s greatest detective happens to be in the vici', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Hercule Poirot (Fictitious character), Private investigators, Belgians, Americans, Archaeologists, Mystery, Large type books, Excavations (Archaeology), Utgrävningar, Skönlitteratur, English literature, Fiction, mystery & detective, general, Private investigators, fiction, Poirot, hercule (fictitious character), fiction, Archaeologists, fiction, Iraq, fiction, Fiction, mystery & detective, traditional, Middle east, fiction, Comic books, strips', 1, '2026-07-21 15:13:37', '2026-07-21 15:13:37'),
(1761, '8b589eed-0b02-41f1-9621-53c9bd570bd6', '9788804519201', 'The Thirteen Problems', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'FONTANA COLLINS', 'OL49134361M', '1932', 'heb', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 221, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'This book consists of several mini stories of unsolved murders and crimes. A group of people each try to solve the mysteries and the person who told the story reveals the true solution.', 'This book consists of several mini stories of unsolved murders and crimes. A group of people each try to solve the mysteries and the person who told the story reveals the true solution.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Jane Marple (Fictitious character), Fiction, Mystery, Suspense fiction, Open Library Staff Picks, English Detective and mystery stories, English Short stories, Translations into French, English fiction, Roman, Roman policier, Français (langue), Lectures et morceaux choisis, Women private investigators, Large type books, England, fiction, Marple, jane (fictitious character), fiction, Fiction, mystery & detective, traditional, Fiction, mystery & detective, women sleuths, Fiction, short stories (single author)', 1, '2026-07-21 15:13:38', '2026-07-21 15:13:38'),
(1762, 'cc33612e-56e5-45dd-9ea9-5fbd26e1fb28', '9782702400500', 'The Moving Finger', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'Harper  Collins', 'OL61439900M', '1942', 'pol', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 224, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'The placid village of Lymstock seems the perfect place for Jerry Burton to recuperate from his accident under the care of his sister, Joanna. But soon a series of vicious poison-pen letters destroys the village\'s quiet charm, eventually causing one recipient to commit suicide. The vicar, the doctor, the servants—all are on the verge of accusing one another when help arrives from an unexpected quarter. The vicar\'s houseguest happens to be none other than Jane Marple.', 'The placid village of Lymstock seems the perfect place for Jerry Burton to recuperate from his accident under the care of his sister, Joanna. But soon a series of vicious poison-pen letters destroys the village\'s quiet charm, eventually causing one recipient to commit suicide. The vicar, the doctor, the servants—all are on the verge of accusing one another when help arrives from an unexpected quarter. The vicar\'s houseguest happens to be none other than Jane Marple.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Women detectives, Jane Marple (Fictitious character), Detective and mystery stories, English fiction, Marple, Jane (Fictitious characters), Mystery, Anonymous letters, Gossip, Large type books, Fiction, mystery & detective, women sleuths, Marple, jane (fictitious character), fiction, Fiction, mystery & detective, general, Women private investigators, Novela policiaca, English literature, Inspectrices de police, Romans, nouvelles, Livres en gros caractères, Large print books', 1, '2026-07-21 15:13:38', '2026-07-21 15:13:38'),
(1763, '426094b3-0775-4283-8052-8adc1202fc49', '9781572707313', 'Mrs. McGinty\'s Dead', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'Harper Paperbacks', 'OL57564184M', '1951', 'chi', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 234, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Poirot, disillusioned by the \"senseless cruel brutality\" of modern crime, pays no attention to the sad case of Mrs McGinty, an old woman apparently struck dead by her lodger for thirty pounds that she kept under a floorboard. When, however, he is asked by the investigating officer to take another look at the case to stop an innocent man going to the gallows, he realises that things may not be as simple as they first appear to be.', 'Poirot, disillusioned by the \"senseless cruel brutality\" of modern crime, pays no attention to the sad case of Mrs McGinty, an old woman apparently struck dead by her lodger for thirty pounds that she kept under a floorboard. When, however, he is asked by the investigating officer to take another look at the case to stop an innocent man going to the gallows, he realises that things may not be as simple as they first appear to be.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Hercule Poirot (Fictitious character), Private investigators, Detective and mystery stories, English Detective and mystery stories, Mystery, Large type books, Fiction, mystery & detective, general, Private investigators, fiction, Poirot, hercule (fictitious character), fiction, Fiction, mystery & detective, traditional, England, fiction, Belgium, fiction, English literature', 1, '2026-07-21 15:13:41', '2026-07-21 15:13:41'),
(1764, 'd73a1dcf-abb8-4ba4-8487-e5d419ac6ab1', '9781539145943', 'Sparkling Cyanide', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'Yuan liu chu ban shi ye gu fen you xian gong si', 'OL58600938M', '1945', 'hin', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 240, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Six people sit down to a sumptuous meal at a table laid for seven. A sprig of rosemary -- \'rosemary for remembrance\' -- marks the empty place. It is the first anniversary of the horrific death by cyanide-laced champagne of the beautiful and troublesome Rosemary Barton. The assembled guests are the same participants at the meal a year prior, and Rosemary\'s widower, George Barton, is determined to prove that one of them is a murderer. But George\'s dinner party, and his plans for justice, will go terribly awry, as another death will come to haunt this date.  Colonel Race of the British Secret Service, friend of Hercule Poirot (and a featured player in Cards on the Table and Death on the Nile), is on the scene to investigate.', 'Six people sit down to a sumptuous meal at a table laid for seven. A sprig of rosemary -- \'rosemary for remembrance\' -- marks the empty place. It is the first anniversary of the horrific death by cyanide-laced champagne of the beautiful and troublesome Rosemary Barton. The assembled guests are the same participants at the meal a year prior, and Rosemary\'s widower, George Barton, is determined to prove that one of them is a murderer. But George\'s dinner party, and his plans for justice, will go t', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction in Spanish, Murder, Rosemary, Fiction, Detective and mystery stories, Mystery fiction, Large type books, Nightclubs, Cocktails, Investigation, English language, Fiction, mystery & detective, general, English literature, Fiction, mystery & detective, traditional, England, fiction, Race, colonel johnny (fictitious character), fiction, Poisoning, Cyanides, English fiction, Translations into Hindi', 1, '2026-07-21 15:13:42', '2026-07-21 15:13:42'),
(1765, '5fe45625-b61c-43f5-89f9-452f9fd671d3', '9780061741005', 'Curtain', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'Perfect Bound', 'OL55756085M', '1975', 'gre', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 232, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'wheelchair-bound Poirot returns to Styles, the venue of his first investigation, where he knows another murder is going to take place…\r\n\r\nThe house guests at Styles seemed perfectly pleasant to Captain Hastings; there was his own daughter Judith, an inoffensive ornithologist called Norton, dashing Mr Allerton, brittle Miss Cole, Doctor Franklin and his fragile wife Barbara , Nurse Craven, Colonel Luttrell and his charming wife, Daisy, and the charismatic Boyd-Carrington.\r\n\r\nSo Hastings was shocked to learn from Hercule Poirot’s declaration that one of them was a five-times murderer. True, the ageing detective was crippled with arthritis, but had his deductive instincts finally deserted him?…', 'wheelchair-bound Poirot returns to Styles, the venue of his first investigation, where he knows another murder is going to take place…\r\n\r\nThe house guests at Styles seemed perfectly pleasant to Captain Hastings; there was his own daughter Judith, an inoffensive ornithologist called Norton, dashing Mr Allerton, brittle Miss Cole, Doctor Franklin and his fragile wife Barbara , Nurse Craven, Colonel Luttrell and his charming wife, Daisy, and the charismatic Boyd-Carrington.\r\n\r\nSo Hastings was shock', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Hercule Poirot (Fictitious character), Private investigators, Detective and mystery stories, Murderers, Country homes, English Detective and mystery stories, English fiction, Mystery, Large type books, Russian language edition, Private investigators in fiction, Fiction, mystery & detective, traditional, Poirot, hercule (fictitious character), fiction, England, fiction, Hastings, arthur, captain (fictitious character), fiction, Detectives, Détectives, Romans, nouvelles, Hercule Poirot (Fictional character)', 1, '2026-07-21 15:13:43', '2026-07-21 15:13:43'),
(1766, '7f553c10-3fec-44d0-8530-12d867d0e353', '9780007120970', 'A Pocket Full of Rye', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'Librairie des Champs-Elysees', 'OL61523517M', '1953', 'heb', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 203, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'En el asesinato de Rex Fortescue todas las pistas señalan a un mismo culpable. La intervención de Miss Marple, recordando una vieja canción de cuna, permite esclarecer los hechos.', 'En el asesinato de Rex Fortescue todas las pistas señalan a un mismo culpable. La intervención de Miss Marple, recordando una vieja canción de cuna, permite esclarecer los hechos.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Ficción, Fiction, Jane Marple (Fictitious character), Marple, Jane (Personaje literario), Novela de misterio, Women detectives, English Detective and mystery stories, Large type books, Murder, Investigation, English literature, Fiction, mystery & detective, women sleuths, Marple, jane (fictitious character), fiction, England, fiction, Fiction, mystery & detective, traditional, Fiction, mystery & detective, general', 1, '2026-07-21 15:13:46', '2026-07-21 15:13:46'),
