(1794, '177a7742-c91b-4128-887d-82c400bdd068', '9780006531142', 'Come, tell me how you live', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'William Morrow', 'OL62084302M', '1946', 'pol', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 208, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Agatha Christie was already a celebrated writer of mysteries in 1930 when she married archaeologist Max Mallowan. She enthusiastically joined him on archaeological expeditions in the Middle East, providing backgrounds for novels and \"everyday doings and happenings\". Pre-war Syria years are remembered here, not chronologically, but in a cluster of vignettes about servants and aristocrats who peppered their lives with annoyances and pleasures.', 'Agatha Christie was already a celebrated writer of mysteries in 1930 when she married archaeologist Max Mallowan. She enthusiastically joined him on archaeological expeditions in the Middle East, providing backgrounds for novels and \"everyday doings and happenings\". Pre-war Syria years are remembered here, not chronologically, but in a cluster of vignettes about servants and aristocrats who peppered their lives with annoyances and pleasures.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Social life and customs, Excavations (Archaeology), Biography, English Authors, Journeys, Travel, English Novelists, Manners and customs, Social life and customs.#x1E; 0., Social life and customs.#x1E; 7., Fouilles archéologiques, Moeurs et coutumes, Récits personnels, [document], Christie, agatha, 1891-1976, Women authors, Authors, biography, Syria, description and travel, English literature, Document', 1, '2026-07-21 15:14:20', '2026-07-21 15:14:20'),
(1795, '1e6d8374-553b-490e-8c0f-c61748490384', '9784150401054', 'Giant\'s bread', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'Fontana', 'OL57586594M', '1929', 'Anglais', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 378, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'A spellbinding novel of romantic obsession. Vernon Deyre is a sensitive and brilliant musician, even a genius. But there is a high price to be paid for his talent, especially by his family and the two women in his life. His sheltered childhood in the home he loves has not prepared Vernon for the harsh reality of his adult years, and in order to write the great masterpiece of his life, he has to make a crucial decision with no time left to count the cost... Famous for her ingenious crime books and plays, Agatha Christie also wrote about crimes of the heart, six bittersweet and very personal novels, as compelling and memorable as the best of her work.', 'A spellbinding novel of romantic obsession. Vernon Deyre is a sensitive and brilliant musician, even a genius. But there is a high price to be paid for his talent, especially by his family and the two women in his life. His sheltered childhood in the home he loves has not prepared Vernon for the harsh reality of his adult years, and in order to write the great masterpiece of his life, he has to make a crucial decision with no time left to count the cost... Famous for her ingenious crime books an', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Composers, Fiction, romance, English literature, Fiction, mystery & detective, general, Fiction, general', 1, '2026-07-21 15:14:21', '2026-07-21 15:14:21'),
