(1927, '520952cf-7ce5-432f-ba06-e336dae534a3', '9780754011507', 'The harlequin tea set and other stories [9 stories]', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'Center Point Large Print', 'OL37775886M', '1997', 'Anglais', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 224, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'The Harlequin Tea Set is a short story collection written by Agatha Christie and first published in the US by G. P. Putnam\'s Sons on April 14, 1997. It contains nine short stories each of which involves a separate mystery. With the exception of The Harlequin Tea Set, which was published in the collection Problem at Pollensa Bay, all stories were published in the UK in 1997 in the anthology While the Light Lasts and Other Stories.\r\n\r\nThe collection of nine stories include:\r\n\r\n    \"The Edge\"\r\n    \"The Actress\"\r\n    \"While the Light Lasts\"\r\n    \"The House of Dreams\"\r\n    \"The Lonely God\"\r\n    \"Manx Gold\"\r\n    \"Within a Wall\"\r\n    \"The Mystery of the Spanish Chest\" (a Hercule Poirot story)\r\n    \"The Harlequin Tea Set\" (a Harley Quin story)', 'The Harlequin Tea Set is a short story collection written by Agatha Christie and first published in the US by G. P. Putnam\'s Sons on April 14, 1997. It contains nine short stories each of which involves a separate mystery. With the exception of The Harlequin Tea Set, which was published in the collection Problem at Pollensa Bay, all stories were published in the UK in 1997 in the anthology While the Light Lasts and Other Stories.\r\n\r\nThe collection of nine stories include:\r\n\r\n    \"The Edge\"', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Detective and mystery stories, Open Library Staff Picks, English Detective and mystery stories, Short stories, Large type books, English literature, Fiction, mystery & detective, traditional, Poirot, hercule (fictitious character), fiction, Fiction, short stories (single author), England, fiction', 1, '2026-07-21 15:17:59', '2026-07-21 15:17:59'),
