(2080, '90f2cf80-6090-4f1f-a9c5-b79a544d2da4', '9780345310132', 'The case of the buried clock', NULL, 'Erle Stanley Gardner', 'Amereon Limited', 'OL58716667M', '1943', 'Anglais', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 245, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'After catching his son-in-law embezzling, wealthy banker Vincent Blane is shocked when the younger man is murdered and Blane\'s daughter is accused, prompting him to call in Perry Mason for her defense.\r\nA buried clock appears, disappears, and re-appears.\r\nIt is set to sidereal time -- the time used by the stars as opposed to the Earth. The book explains this.\r\nBut who did it? And why? And when? And where?\r\nSo much to discover -- so little time when two defendants are being tried and neither will talk to Perry. Not even the one who is his client.', 'After catching his son-in-law embezzling, wealthy banker Vincent Blane is shocked when the younger man is murdered and Blane\'s daughter is accused, prompting him to call in Perry Mason for her defense.\r\nA buried clock appears, disappears, and re-appears.\r\nIt is set to sidereal time -- the time used by the stars as opposed to the Earth. The book explains this.\r\nBut who did it? And why? And when? And where?\r\nSo much to discover -- so little time when two defendants are being tried and neither will', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Large type books, Perry Mason (Fictitious character), Trials (Murder), American Detective and mystery stories, Translations into Russian', 1, '2026-07-21 15:22:00', '2026-07-21 15:22:00'),
