(2137, '25513542-53d6-45f9-935c-5f28148f6ad5', '9780345362209', 'The case of the daring decoy', NULL, 'Erle Stanley Gardner', 'Ulverscroft', 'OL59562824M', '1957', 'jpn', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 224, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0, 0, 'Perry Mason (Fictitious character), Fiction, Detective and mystery stories', 1, '2026-07-21 15:23:38', '2026-07-21 15:23:38'),
(2138, '19b870cb-381d-4453-a0eb-ed2eba2a5961', '9788427207431', 'The case of the careless cupid', NULL, 'Erle Stanley Gardner', 'House of Stratus', 'OL13227453M', '1968', 'Anglais', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 224, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '**BLACK WIDOW**\r\nThere\'s no love lost between Delane Arlington\'s fiancée and his frosty family. The wealthy widower\'s heirs are extremely eager to keep their lovestruck uncle from tying the knot - and thus cutting off their route to easy street. That\'s what brings Selma Anson, Arlington\'s beleaguered bride-to-be, to Perry Mason\'s office.\r\n\r\nWise investment of her late husband\'s insurance made Selma a well-off widow. But her prospective new groom\'s avaricious nieces and nephews have her pegged as a gold digger - *and* a gravedigger! They\'re determined to prove that Selma poisoned her first husband. Mason is equally determined to prove them liars. But when damning evidence turns up - and Selma takes off - it could make Perry\'s defense deadly difficult...', '**BLACK WIDOW**\r\nThere\'s no love lost between Delane Arlington\'s fiancée and his frosty family. The wealthy widower\'s heirs are extremely eager to keep their lovestruck uncle from tying the knot - and thus cutting off their route to easy street. That\'s what brings Selma Anson, Arlington\'s beleaguered bride-to-be, to Perry Mason\'s office.\r\n\r\nWise investment of her late husband\'s insurance made Selma a well-off widow. But her prospective new groom\'s avaricious nieces and nephews have her pegged as', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Perry Mason (Fictitious character), Fiction, Mason, Perry (Fictitious character), Trials (Murder), Large type books, Fiction in English, California, fiction, Lawyers, fiction, Los angeles (calif.), fiction, Mason, perry (fictitious character), fiction, Fiction, legal, Fiction, mystery & detective, general', 1, '2026-07-21 15:23:39', '2026-07-21 15:23:39'),
(2139, 'f8da1f56-ec94-43f1-8503-01b56c314428', '9780330021494', 'The case of the duplicate daughter', NULL, 'Erle Stanley Gardner', 'Morrow', 'OL49217266M', '1960', 'Anglais', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 224, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'A daughter comes to Mason for help when her father goes missing at breakfast and when she looks for him, discovers a pool of blood in his workshop and several one hundred dollar bills. Twins separated at birth and a blackmail stir up a murder and Perry Mason has to defend the daughter against murder charges.', 'A daughter comes to Mason for help when her father goes missing at breakfast and when she looks for him, discovers a pool of blood in his workshop and several one hundred dollar bills. Twins separated at birth and a blackmail stir up a murder and Perry Mason has to defend the daughter against murder charges.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, American fiction, Perry Mason (Fictitious character), Large type books, Fiction, mystery & detective, general, Fiction, legal, Mason, perry (fictitious character), fiction, Lawyers, fiction, California, fiction, Los angeles (calif.), fiction', 1, '2026-07-21 15:23:39', '2026-07-21 15:23:39'),
(2140, '2f78de40-20ce-42b9-ad1d-fd0f4c57f7c9', '9789350261293', 'The case of the singing skirt', NULL, 'Erle Stanley Gardner', 'Morrow', 'OL49229541M', '1959', 'Allemand', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 221, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'ix, 313 p. (large print) ; 22 cm', 'ix, 313 p. (large print) ; 22 cm', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Perry Mason (Fictitious character), Trials (Murder), Fiction, Large type books, Mason, Perry (Fictitious character) -- Fiction', 1, '2026-07-21 15:23:42', '2026-07-21 15:23:42'),
(2141, 'accfeb37-9d8d-47c1-af68-533a4d57552b', '9780345308818', 'The Case of the Dubious Bridegroom', NULL, 'Erle Stanley Gardner', 'Ballantine Books', 'OL58743047M', '1949', 'gre', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 213, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Paul Drake\'s voice came over the wire so fast that the words seemed to telescope into each other. \r\n     \"Get this Perry, and get it fast,\" he said. \"We\'re sitting on a keg of dynamite. My man found Ethel Garvin dead as a mackerel, sitting in her automobile with a bullet hole in her left temple.\" \r\n\r\n\"Suicide?\" asked Perry Mason. \r\n\"Not much chance,\" Drake continued. \r\n\"She\'s slumped over the steering wheel and it\'s rather messy. The gun is lying on the ground directly beneath the window.\"\r\n     \"What about the police?\"\r\n     \"My operative discovered the body and managed to notify me. He\'s notifying the sheriff and the coroner\'s office. He got the number of the gun and I\'m trying to trace it. We may be just one step ahead of the police.\"\r\n     \"Okay,\" said Perry Mason. \"Stay one step ahead of them. I\'m on my way.\"\r\n     But neither Paul Drake nor Perry Mason was fast enough to stay one step ahead. And only a seemingly miraculous piece of detective work kept Perry Mason\'s client from being convicted of murder-and Perry from being disbarred.', 'Paul Drake\'s voice came over the wire so fast that the words seemed to telescope into each other. \r\n     \"Get this Perry, and get it fast,\" he said. \"We\'re sitting on a keg of dynamite. My man found Ethel Garvin dead as a mackerel, sitting in her automobile with a bullet hole in her left temple.\" \r\n\r\n\"Suicide?\" asked Perry Mason. \r\n\"Not much chance,\" Drake continued. \r\n\"She\'s slumped over the steering wheel and it\'s rather messy. The gun is lying on the ground directly beneath the window.\"', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, American Detective and mystery stories, Perry Mason (Fictitious character), Translations into Russian, Large type books, Detective and mystery stories', 1, '2026-07-21 15:23:43', '2026-07-21 15:23:43'),
(2142, 'f13c336a-69f5-4a60-ab96-53fd02e83961', '9780857683168', 'Top of the heap', NULL, 'Erle Stanley Gardner', 'W. J. Black', 'OL59783845M', '1952', 'Anglais', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 222, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '**Cool & Lam Mystery #13** (1952)\r\n\r\nJohn Carver Billings II has a story with more holes in it than the surgeons had to sew up in the torso of recuperating LA Mob boss Gabby Garvanza. On the other hand, Billings has also promised Bertha Cool a $500 bonus on top of the usual agency fees. Donald Lam\'s concerns fall on ears deafened by the sound of Bertha\'s office cash drawer slamming shut on Billings\' initial payment of $300 in cold, hard cash. Not that their client is in any way implicated in the botched Garvanza hit. Billings\' style runs more to hitting on attractive women in cocktail lounges. Twice in short order, according to him. \"Morrie\" was the first pick-up. Billings swears he didn\'t know she was in fact Maurine Auburn, Gabby Garvanza\'s girlfriend and a witness to his unfortunate encounter with a lead double-tap. Didn\'t learn anything about that side of things until days later, when the newspapers reported her mysterious disappearance--after a cocktail lounge pick-up separated her from her companions. But she isn\'t the missing person Billings wants the agency to find. He claims she ditched him almost immediately, and he then moved on to a twosome, \"Sylvia\" and \"Millie.\" That\'s where his tale really starts leaking like a sieve. He says flat-out that he\'s paying Cool & Lam to deliver Sylvia and Millie as an alibi. It\'s the gaps between his words that have Donald Lam hearing alarm bells.', '**Cool & Lam Mystery #13** (1952)\r\n\r\nJohn Carver Billings II has a story with more holes in it than the surgeons had to sew up in the torso of recuperating LA Mob boss Gabby Garvanza. On the other hand, Billings has also promised Bertha Cool a $500 bonus on top of the usual agency fees. Donald Lam\'s concerns fall on ears deafened by the sound of Bertha\'s office cash drawer slamming shut on Billings\' initial payment of $300 in cold, hard cash. Not that their client is in any way implicated in the', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, mystery & detective, general, Missing persons, fiction, Crime, fiction, Donald Lam (Fictitious character), Fiction, Private investigators, Missing persons, Investigation', 1, '2026-07-21 15:23:43', '2026-07-21 15:23:43'),
(2143, 'dcb79dff-3329-43ed-b1f1-6e269020b3d2', '9780007284191', 'Detectives And Young Adventurers The Complete Short Stories', NULL, 'Agatha Christie', 'HarperCollins Publishers', 'OL25975948M', '2008', 'Anglais', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', NULL, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, mystery & detective, collections & anthologies', 1, '2026-07-21 15:23:44', '2026-07-21 15:23:44'),
(2144, 'b9166507-57ee-4c2a-8742-4cbef562e514', '9780671755621', 'The Case of the Waylaid Wolf', NULL, 'Erle Stanley Gardner', 'THE THRILLER BOOK CLUB', 'OL58743209M', '1959', 'Anglais', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 213, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '*\"Come on, baby,\" he said, \"don\'t be a prude.\"*\r\n\r\nHe kept on advancing, his face no longer a mask of affability but filled with savage, primitive, ruthless passion.\r\n\r\nSeething with indignation, Arlene attacked him. But with brutal strength he pushed her back until she collapsed on the davenport.\r\n\r\nShe doubled her knees, got them against his chest and gave a sudden push. As he staggered to his feet, she picked up a chair and threw it. It caught him low in the abdomen and he doubled over in pain.\r\n\r\nArlene grabbed her raincoat and made for the door, running down the gravel driveway, past the swimming pool, out to the dirt road.\r\n\r\nWhen she could run no more, she looked back. The beam of headlights was swinging around the driveway. Then the car started slowly down the road after her...\r\n\r\nIf you\'re young, attractive, and female, resist the advances of Loring Lamont at your peril. The spoiled son of a rich and powerful father, Lamont is a wolf who goes after one pretty lamb too many. For stenographer Arlene Ferris has vowed not to let him get away with his cruel come-ons, though she never had murder in mind.\r\n\r\nPerry Mason\'s cardinal rule - always trust your client - finds its sorest test when all the evidence says the unfortunate Miss Ferris brandished the fatal knife. Now he may have to step over the line of the law to prove his trust was justified.', '*\"Come on, baby,\" he said, \"don\'t be a prude.\"*\r\n\r\nHe kept on advancing, his face no longer a mask of affability but filled with savage, primitive, ruthless passion.\r\n\r\nSeething with indignation, Arlene attacked him. But with brutal strength he pushed her back until she collapsed on the davenport.\r\n\r\nShe doubled her knees, got them against his chest and gave a sudden push. As he staggered to his feet, she picked up a chair and threw it. It caught him low in the abdomen and he doubled over in pai', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Perry Mason (Fictitious character), Trials (Murder), Detective and mystery stories', 1, '2026-07-21 15:23:46', '2026-07-21 15:23:46'),
