(2231, 'b0cf072d-aebe-4f8d-80a5-ce40f2fb376a', '9781471909214', 'Cut Thin to Win', NULL, 'Erle Stanley Gardner', 'Walter J. Black', 'OL60720654M', '1965', 'Allemand', 'Agatha Christie', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 192, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '**Cool & Lam Mystery #26** (1965)\r\n\r\nNeither Clayton Dawson nor his tale of wild-child daughter Phyllis and a hypothetical hit-and-run while driving drunk quite rings true. And Dawson makes no secret of the fact that full disclosure on his part could put Cool and Lam in a legal bind. In the course of his visit, however, Dawson has piqued Donald Lam\'s professional pride to the point where there\'s no question of declining the case. Except, sometimes, even the brainiest of investigators can underestimate the duplicity of his clients. Not to mention their associates. Suddenly, Lam\'s PI license and his freedom are both on the line.', '**Cool & Lam Mystery #26** (1965)\r\n\r\nNeither Clayton Dawson nor his tale of wild-child daughter Phyllis and a hypothetical hit-and-run while driving drunk quite rings true. And Dawson makes no secret of the fact that full disclosure on his part could put Cool and Lam in a legal bind. In the course of his visit, however, Dawson has piqued Donald Lam\'s professional pride to the point where there\'s no question of declining the case. Except, sometimes, even the brainiest of investigators can underes', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, crime, Fiction, mystery & detective, general, Donald Lam (Fictitious character), Fiction, Murder, Investigation, Private investigators', 1, '2026-07-21 15:27:45', '2026-07-21 15:27:45'),
(2232, '77e4d1ad-f0a7-4477-947f-2f7d2638b58a', '9781471909115', 'Bachelors get lonely', NULL, 'Erle Stanley Gardner', 'Morrow', 'OL53227032M', '1961', 'Anglais', 'Agatha Christie', 'other', 'paperback', 'all', 192, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Two incidents involving a Peeping Tom are reported from the Swim and Tan Motel to the detective agency belonging to Donald Lam and Bertha Cool. Bertha, meanwhile, has warned Donald to steer clear of the dangerous jobs and stick to aiding solid, sane citizens like Montrose L. Carson. And all Carson wants is the name of the informer in his office who is passing on confidential material to a business rival, Herbert Dowling.\r\nBut when Dowling is murdered at the Swim and Tan Motel, it looks as though Bertha has picked the wrong client, and Donald the right girl when he chooses a lively bait to catch the Peeping Tom ... and the murderer.', 'Two incidents involving a Peeping Tom are reported from the Swim and Tan Motel to the detective agency belonging to Donald Lam and Bertha Cool. Bertha, meanwhile, has warned Donald to steer clear of the dangerous jobs and stick to aiding solid, sane citizens like Montrose L. Carson. And all Carson wants is the name of the informer in his office who is passing on confidential material to a business rival, Herbert Dowling.\r\nBut when Dowling is murdered at the Swim and Tan Motel, it looks as though', 0.00, 0, 0, NULL, 1, '2026-07-21 15:27:46', '2026-07-21 15:27:46'),
