(2787, '636af3bc-607f-4d68-a18b-ea79dbb0fc2b', '9781299456778', 'The lion\'s world', NULL, 'Rowan Williams', 'SPCK Publishing', 'OL46091039M', '2012', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'religious', 'paperback', 'all', 164, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '\"This compelling account of the Narnia novels unlocks their Christian symbolism and explores the moral and spiritual wisdom that C. S. Lewis intended to convey. From the introduction: \'I want to capture something of what Lewis is trying to do in communicating - to a world that frequently thinks is knows what faith is - the character, the feel, of a real experience of surrender in the face of absolute incarnate love\'. \" --Publisher description.', '\"This compelling account of the Narnia novels unlocks their Christian symbolism and explores the moral and spiritual wisdom that C. S. Lewis intended to convey. From the introduction: \'I want to capture something of what Lewis is trying to do in communicating - to a world that frequently thinks is knows what faith is - the character, the feel, of a real experience of surrender in the face of absolute incarnate love\'. \" --Publisher description.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Lewis, c. s. (clive staples), 1898-1963, Narnia (imaginary place), Christian literature, Irish literature, history and criticism, Criticism and interpretation, Christianity and literature', 1, '2026-07-21 15:43:17', '2026-07-21 15:43:17'),
