(2801, '16915e09-9c89-4d8f-8216-b435e9c1870d', '9780802876560', 'Being Human', NULL, 'Rowan Williams', 'Eerdmans', 'OL27359099M', '2018', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'religious', 'paperback', 'all', 127, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'What is consciousness? Is the mind a machine? What makes us persons? How can we find the path to human maturity? These are among the fundamental questions that Rowan Williams helps us to think about in this deeply engaging exploration oof what it means to be human. The book ends with a brief but profound meditation on the person of Christ, inviting us to consider how, through him, \'our humanity in all its variety, in all its vulnerability, has been taken into the heart of the divine life\'. With discussion questions for personal or group use at the end of each chapter, this is a book that readers of all religious persuasions will find both challenging and highly rewarding.', 'What is consciousness? Is the mind a machine? What makes us persons? How can we find the path to human maturity? These are among the fundamental questions that Rowan Williams helps us to think about in this deeply engaging exploration oof what it means to be human. The book ends with a brief but profound meditation on the person of Christ, inviting us to consider how, through him, \'our humanity in all its variety, in all its vulnerability, has been taken into the heart of the divine life\'. With', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Consciousness, Christian life, Human body, Christianity, Mind and body, Religious aspects', 1, '2026-07-21 15:43:36', '2026-07-21 15:43:36'),
(2802, 'ba47a5ca-c6e3-4c5c-ac3c-bf836afdbf95', '9781408187593', 'Faith in the public square', NULL, 'Rowan Williams', 'Bloomsbury Publishing Plc', 'OL48644036M', '2012', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'other', 'paperback', 'all', 348, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'This book contains critical commentary on contemporary issues by Rowan Williams, in his final book as Archbishop of Canterbury. Archbishop Rowan Williams is the most gifted Anglican priest of his generation. His views are consistent and orthodox and yet he has been consistently misunderstood - especially in relation to his views on contemporary society, public morality and the common good. In this, the final published work of his Archepiscopate, Dr. Williams has assembled a series of chapters on matters of immediate public concern and the relationship of Christianity to these issues.', 'This book contains critical commentary on contemporary issues by Rowan Williams, in his final book as Archbishop of Canterbury. Archbishop Rowan Williams is the most gifted Anglican priest of his generation. His views are consistent and orthodox and yet he has been consistently misunderstood - especially in relation to his views on contemporary society, public morality and the common good. In this, the final published work of his Archepiscopate, Dr. Williams has assembled a series of chapters on', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Social conditions, Anglican Communion, Church and social problems', 1, '2026-07-21 15:43:38', '2026-07-21 15:43:38'),
