(2825, 'cec5124c-2f0e-4507-af99-26189b8490c0', '9780230251908', 'Crisis and recovery', NULL, 'Rowan Williams, Larry Elliott', 'Palgrave Macmillan', 'OL39515825M', '2010', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'other', 'paperback', 'all', 344, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '\"During the ongoing global financial crisis, a lack of moral and ethical leadership in society has been exposed. The Most Reverend Rowan Williams, Archbishop of Canterbury and Larry Elliott, The Guardian, bring together their thoughts on the issues of ethics and morality in business, with contributions from leading business figures\"-- Provided by publisher.', '\"During the ongoing global financial crisis, a lack of moral and ethical leadership in society has been exposed. The Most Reverend Rowan Williams, Archbishop of Canterbury and Larry Elliott, The Guardian, bring together their thoughts on the issues of ethics and morality in business, with contributions from leading business figures\"-- Provided by publisher.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Global Financial Crisis, 2008-2009, Moral and ethical aspects, Religious aspects, Financial crises, Economic conditions, Economics, Leadership, Business ethics, Success in business, Economics, moral and ethical aspects, Great britain, economic conditions, Macroeconomics, General, Public finance, Management, Business & economics -> management -> business ethics, Business & economics -> economics -> principles of macroeconomics, Cs.soc_sci.poli_sci.gen_polit_sc, Business & economics -> economics -> public finance, Business & economics -> management -> principles of management', 1, '2026-07-21 15:44:18', '2026-07-21 15:44:18'),
(2826, 'cb07c027-a215-4f0b-885f-ac35a56c3b7f', '9781322373355', 'Meeting God in Mark', NULL, 'Rowan Williams', 'Westminster John Knox Press', 'OL34011147M', '2014', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'religious', 'paperback', 'all', 86, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Meeting God in Mark explores the essential meaning and purpose of Mark\'s Gospel for beginners who may be curious about the Gospels and want to learn more, as well as for those who\'ve read the Gospel many times before and want to see it in a fresh light. This beautifully written book by beloved Anglican Rowan Williams, former Archbishop of Canterbury, is packed with illuminating spiritual insights, and the focus on the Passion narrative makes this ideal as a Lenten devotional or study resource. Each of the three chapters includes questions for reflection. The end of the book includes a reading guide, reflection, and prayer for each of the seven weeks of Lent. (Publisher).', 'Meeting God in Mark explores the essential meaning and purpose of Mark\'s Gospel for beginners who may be curious about the Gospels and want to learn more, as well as for those who\'ve read the Gospel many times before and want to see it in a fresh light. This beautifully written book by beloved Anglican Rowan Williams, former Archbishop of Canterbury, is packed with illuminating spiritual insights, and the focus on the Passion narrative makes this ideal as a Lenten devotional or study resource. E', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Bible, Bible, criticism, interpretation, etc., n. t. gospels, Bible, meditations, n. t., Meditations', 1, '2026-07-21 15:44:19', '2026-07-21 15:44:19'),
(2827, '02c98542-47ea-4d63-8f18-bf727121cd44', '9781472945532', 'Christ the Heart of Creation', NULL, 'Rowan Williams', 'Bloomsbury Publishing Plc', 'OL48670529M', '2018', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'religious', 'paperback', 'all', 304, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '\"In this wide-ranging book, Rowan Williams argues that what we say about Jesus Christ is key to understanding what Christian belief says about creator and creation overall. Through detailed discussion of texts from the earliest centuries to the present day, we are shown some of the various and subtle ways in which Christians have discovered in their reflections on Christ the possibility of a deeply affirmative approach to creation, and a set of radical insights in ethics and politics as well. Throughout his life, Rowan Williams has been deeply influenced by thinkers of the Eastern Christian tradition as well as Catholic and Anglican writers. This book draws on insights from Eastern Christianity, from the Western Middle Ages and from Reformed thinkers, from Calvin to Bonhoeffer - as well as considering theological insights sparked by philosophers like Kierkegaard and Wittgenstein. Christ the Heart of Creation concerns fundamental issues for Christian belief and Williams tackles them head-on: he writes with pellucid clarity and shows his gift for putting across what are inevitably complex ideas to a wide audience.\"--Bloomsbury Publishing.', '\"In this wide-ranging book, Rowan Williams argues that what we say about Jesus Christ is key to understanding what Christian belief says about creator and creation overall. Through detailed discussion of texts from the earliest centuries to the present day, we are shown some of the various and subtle ways in which Christians have discovered in their reflections on Christ the possibility of a deeply affirmative approach to creation, and a set of radical insights in ethics and politics as well. Th', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Jesus christ, person and offices, Creation, RELIGION / Christian Theology / Systematic, Thomas, aquinas, saint, 1225?-1274, Christianity, Religious ethics, Religion and politics, Primacy, Person and offices', 1, '2026-07-21 15:44:21', '2026-07-21 15:44:21'),
