(2835, 'c2621afe-fe67-47a2-be49-81f518cf4d39', '9780664262648', 'The Sign and the Sacrifice', NULL, 'Rowan Williams', 'Westminster John Knox Press', 'OL37860003M', '2017', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'religious', 'paperback', 'all', 114, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Rowan Williams, former Archbishop of Canterbury, presents the Gospel accounts of Jesus\' crucifixion and resurrection as viewed through the eyes of those who witnessed them. The Sign and the Sacrifice explores the meaning of the cross and the significance of Christ\'s resurrection, discussing what these events meant to Jesus\' followers in the early years and what they can say to us today.', 'Rowan Williams, former Archbishop of Canterbury, presents the Gospel accounts of Jesus\' crucifixion and resurrection as viewed through the eyes of those who witnessed them. The Sign and the Sacrifice explores the meaning of the cross and the significance of Christ\'s resurrection, discussing what these events meant to Jesus\' followers in the early years and what they can say to us today.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Crucifixion, Theology of the cross, Resurrection, Crucifixion of Jesus Christ, Resurrection of Jesus Christ', 1, '2026-07-21 15:44:32', '2026-07-21 15:44:32'),
(2836, '913f416f-d613-42ab-b67a-9dffa5ba588c', '9781471254161', 'The woman who walked into the sea', NULL, 'Mark Douglas-Home', 'Sandstone', 'OL28583445M', '2013', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 340, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Cal McGill watches the young woman through the dirty windscreen of his Toyota. There\'s something compelling about her stillness, about the length of time she has been standing square-shouldered, erect, staring out to sea, like an Antony Gormley statue waiting for another of its cast-iron tribe to emerge from the deep. What has brought her to this remote beach, he asks himself. Is she a kindred spirit who finds refuge by the shore? Idle curiosity soon turns into another investigation for oceanographer and loner McGill as he embarks on a quest to discover why, 26 years earlier, another young woman walked accross this sweep of sand and into the waves, apparently drowning herself and her unborn child.', 'Cal McGill watches the young woman through the dirty windscreen of his Toyota. There\'s something compelling about her stillness, about the length of time she has been standing square-shouldered, erect, staring out to sea, like an Antony Gormley statue waiting for another of its cast-iron tribe to emerge from the deep. What has brought her to this remote beach, he asks himself. Is she a kindred spirit who finds refuge by the shore? Idle curiosity soon turns into another investigation for oceanogr', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Fiction, Murder, Investigation, Oceanographers, Fiction, mystery & detective, general, Fiction, crime', 1, '2026-07-21 15:44:32', '2026-07-21 15:44:32'),
