(3183, '498876bc-f18a-480e-9947-f2b14fbaf541', '9781847822192', 'One step too far', NULL, 'Lauran Paine', 'Linford', 'OL32363515M', '2008', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 186, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Claire Escott had ignored her father\'s warning against involvement with her fiance, Mark Rowland. However, she little realized the extent of the scientist\'s corroding ambition. And it was not long after their marriage that Rowland\'s ruthless pursuit of a scientific empire encompassed a horrifying murder. But that was only the start of things.', 'Claire Escott had ignored her father\'s warning against involvement with her fiance, Mark Rowland. However, she little realized the extent of the scientist\'s corroding ambition. And it was not long after their marriage that Rowland\'s ruthless pursuit of a scientific empire encompassed a horrifying murder. But that was only the start of things.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Ambition, Fiction, Scientists', 1, '2026-07-21 15:55:25', '2026-07-21 15:55:25'),
(3184, '5f14bb02-6cbe-4a56-9b6c-615ca4c11229', '9781444803815', 'Endless day', NULL, 'Lauran Paine', 'Linford', 'OL32096610M', '2010', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'other', 'paperback', 'all', 184, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '\"It\'s June 30th. And in Annex 10, situated in the Adirondack Mountains of New York, scientist Dr. Gray and his team can hardly believe their instrument readings. It\'s four o\'clock, and as the seconds pass, they see that chaos looms for mankind. The Earth is growing hotter, temperatures rocket, as the sun shines through the night and causes endless days. Everyone suffers - the rich, the poor, the criminal and the family man. Will it ever end?\"--BOOK COVER.', '\"It\'s June 30th. And in Annex 10, situated in the Adirondack Mountains of New York, scientist Dr. Gray and his team can hardly believe their instrument readings. It\'s four o\'clock, and as the seconds pass, they see that chaos looms for mankind. The Earth is growing hotter, temperatures rocket, as the sun shines through the night and causes endless days. Everyone suffers - the rich, the poor, the criminal and the family man. Will it ever end?\"--BOOK COVER.', 0.00, 0, 0, NULL, 1, '2026-07-21 15:55:26', '2026-07-21 15:55:26'),
(3185, '75c4ab54-41b6-4cd7-b2a7-426904ec1a79', '9781847827128', 'Man of two worlds', NULL, 'Lauran Paine', 'Linford/Thorpe', 'OL32348055M', '2009', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 236, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '\"Walter Cardish was a very ordinary, somewhat downtrodden individual. But, following an incredible accident, he recovers in hospital and finds that he has been granted the power of seeing into the future. Assuming the identity of \'The Great Volta: Prognosticator\' he amasses a fortune, and a reputation as a seer. But his activities also create enemies, and soon one of them tries to kill him, and the implacable workings of his strange destiny close in upon him inexorably.\"--Page 4 of cover.', '\"Walter Cardish was a very ordinary, somewhat downtrodden individual. But, following an incredible accident, he recovers in hospital and finds that he has been granted the power of seeing into the future. Assuming the identity of \'The Great Volta: Prognosticator\' he amasses a fortune, and a reputation as a seer. But his activities also create enemies, and soon one of them tries to kill him, and the implacable workings of his strange destiny close in upon him inexorably.\"--Page 4 of cover.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Prophets, Fiction', 1, '2026-07-21 15:55:27', '2026-07-21 15:55:27'),
(3186, '8826a79f-9428-4249-890f-9a93ec1ccc6c', '9781847829795', 'The lie destroyer', NULL, 'Lauran Paine', 'Thorpe', 'OL32120582M', '2010', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'science', 'paperback', 'all', 240, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Bobby Carson is proud of his lying expertise. His scientist father uses him as a guinea pig for a machine which destroys his ability to be dishonest, but has unhappy social consequences. Soon criminals begin exploiting the possibilities of a world without lies in a society built upon sham and pretence. And Scotland Yard, hampered by its own guilty secrets, cannot stem the tide of blackmail ... until Dr. Carson, the creator of the Lie Destroyer, again steps into the scene ...', 'Bobby Carson is proud of his lying expertise. His scientist father uses him as a guinea pig for a machine which destroys his ability to be dishonest, but has unhappy social consequences. Soon criminals begin exploiting the possibilities of a world without lies in a society built upon sham and pretence. And Scotland Yard, hampered by its own guilty secrets, cannot stem the tide of blackmail ... until Dr. Carson, the creator of the Lie Destroyer, again steps into the scene ...', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Truthfulness and falsehood, Fiction, Discoveries in science', 1, '2026-07-21 15:55:28', '2026-07-21 15:55:28'),
(3187, '74f4b4a5-2e83-48aa-9f6b-a6a5b7b8a61b', '9781847827517', 'The Atlantic tunnel', NULL, 'Lauran Paine', 'Linford', 'OL32078507M', '2009', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 266, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, 'Deep beneath the floor of the Atlantic Ocean, scientists and engineers attempt the most daring and audacious scientific project of all time: the construction of an undersea tunnel between Great Britain and Canada; linking Land\'s End with Labrador. Canadian and British teams work simultaneously at either end, to converge in the middle. Using scientific methods to fight the crushing pressure and geological and marine perils involved, the brave workers face a far greater hazard - the danger within - from saboteurs!', 'Deep beneath the floor of the Atlantic Ocean, scientists and engineers attempt the most daring and audacious scientific project of all time: the construction of an undersea tunnel between Great Britain and Canada; linking Land\'s End with Labrador. Canadian and British teams work simultaneously at either end, to converge in the middle. Using scientific methods to fight the crushing pressure and geological and marine perils involved, the brave workers face a far greater hazard - the danger within', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Underwater tunnels, Fiction, Design and construction, Sabotage', 1, '2026-07-21 15:55:29', '2026-07-21 15:55:29'),
(3188, '4534acd2-333f-42e5-99a7-30cc39dffafc', '9781847826374', 'The spiked boy', NULL, 'Lauran Paine', 'Linford', 'OL32143695M', '2009', 'Anglais', 'Mark Douglas', 'novel', 'paperback', 'all', 266, 'black_white', NULL, NULL, '\"Dick Palmer and Will Snell are great friends, both former highwaymen who were subsequently exonerated. However, they become fugitives from the law again when members of a mysterious gang of murderers and kidnappers use their names to frame them. Then when the gang kidnap Palmer\'s wife the two friends are plunged into a deadly struggle to rescue her. But they are up against an evil and secret organization - and the sadistic Simon Pendexter, who swings a \'spiked boy\' ...\"--Publisher description.', '\"Dick Palmer and Will Snell are great friends, both former highwaymen who were subsequently exonerated. However, they become fugitives from the law again when members of a mysterious gang of murderers and kidnappers use their names to frame them. Then when the gang kidnap Palmer\'s wife the two friends are plunged into a deadly struggle to rescue her. But they are up against an evil and secret organization - and the sadistic Simon Pendexter, who swings a \'spiked boy\' ...\"--Publisher description.', 0.00, 0, 0, 'Gangs, Fiction, Kidnapping', 1, '2026-07-21 15:55:30', '2026-07-21 15:55:30'),
